WEBVTT

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.030
He wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:34.080
Saving people,hunting
things. The family business.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.780
Today's your lucky day,kid.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.680
You watch out for sammy,okay?
Yeah,dad. You know I will.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.690
Dad.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.210
Time of death -10:41 A.M.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.640
I miss him,man,and I'm not
all right. Neither are you.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:53.620
I'm dealing with dad's death!

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.300
Dad's dead,and it hurts
so bad, you can't take it.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.020
I'm okay! I swear,the next
person who asks if I'm okay,

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.930
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.860
Okay,we got booze...

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.070
We got chocolate...

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.670
And...wait for it.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.300
Tortured emo rock.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.490
Guaranteed cure for any broken heart.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.730
You didn't have to do all this.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.350
I'm fine.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:25.120
Yeah,I can see that.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:30.260
Thanks,neal.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.540
You're a good friend.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:39.950
It's probably him.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.060
I'll take care of it.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:47.350
Where is she?

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.460
Chill out and think about this,okay?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.980
I need to talk to her. Some other time.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.220
You get out of my face now.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.930
Angela?

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.610
Leave...me...alone.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.380
Angela,I'm sorry.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.580
You're sorry?

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:30.840
You're sorry? Oh,that's great.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.190
Angela,listen to me.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.790
I don't want to listen to you!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.540
I'm done listening! Listen to me.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.530
How could you do this? I loved you.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.940
Angela?

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.680
Angela!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.310
Come on,sam. I'm begging
you. This is stupid.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.350
Why?

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.520
Going to visit mom's grave?

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.780
She doesn't even have a grave. There
was no body left after the fire.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.940
She has a headstone.

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:29.150
Put up by our uncle, a
man that we've never met.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.630
You want to pay your respects to a
slab of granite put up by a stranger.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:35.110
That's not the point. Then enlighten me.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:38.100
It's not about a body or a casket.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.900
It's about her memory, okay?

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.500
And after
dad,it just --

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.230
It just feels like
the right thing to do.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.680
It's irrational is what it is.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.300
Look,man, no one asked you to come.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.990
Why don't we swing by
the roadhouse instead?

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.840
We haven't heard anything on the demon lately.
We should be hunting that son of a bitch down.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.430
That's a good idea. You should.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:58.700
Just drop me off,I'll hitch a ride,
and I'll meet you there tomorrow.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.590
Right.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:06.010
Stuck with those people, making
awkward small talk until you show up.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.810
No,thanks.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:42.050
I think,uh...

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.840
I think dad would have
wanted you to have these.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.300
I love you,mom.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.750
Thank you.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.150
Angela mason.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.250
She was a student at the local
college. Her funeral was three days ago.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:31.930
And?

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:33.310
And?

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.860
You saw her grave -- Everything
dead around it in a perfect circle.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.190
You don't think that's a little weird?

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.380
Maybe the grounds keeper went a
little agro with the pesticide.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:44.380
No,I asked him. No pesticide,no
chemicals. Nobody can explain it.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.140
Okay, so,what are you thinking?

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:49.700
I don't know. Unholy ground,maybe.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:52.540
What?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.480
If something evil happened,it
could easily poison the ground.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.880
Remember the farm
outside of cedar rapids?

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:58.580
Yeah.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.670
It could be the sign
of a demonic presence

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.470
Or the angela girl's spirit,
if it's powerful enough.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.410
Well,don't get too excited.
You might pull something.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:12.540
It's just stumbling onto a hunt...

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.400
Here of all places? So?

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:18.920
So,are you sure this is about
a hunt,not something else?

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.390
What else would it be about?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.500
Just forget it.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:25.550
Believe what you want,sam,

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:29.670
But I let you drag my ass out here.
The least we can do is check this out.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:34.060
Yeah,fine.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.070
The girl's dad works in town.
He's a professor at the school.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.460
Dr. Mason? Yes.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.000
I'm sam. This is dean.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.050
We were friends of angela'S.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:02.670
We -We wanted to offer our condolences.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.070
Please come in.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.170
She was beautiful.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.250
Yes,she was.

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:22.070
This is an unusual book.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:28.340
It's ancient greek. I teach a course.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.750
So,a car accident.
That's -That's horrible.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:42.610
Angie was only a mile
away from home when...

00:17:44.039 --> 00:17:48.630
It's got to be hard...
losing someone like that.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:52.950
Sometimes it's like
they're still around,

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:57.160
Almost like you can still
sense their presence.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.930
You ever feel anything like that?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.760
I do,as a matter of fact.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:06.620
That's perfectly normal, dr. Mason,

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.940
Especially with what
you're going through.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.789
You know, I still phone her.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:18.079
And the phone's ringing
before I remember that,uh...

00:18:20.789 --> 00:18:23.450
Family's everything, you know?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.660
Angie was the most
important thing in my life.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:31.550
And now I'm just lost without her.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:39.670
I'm very sorry.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:43.720
There's something going on.
We just haven't found it yet.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:48.210
Dean,so far you got a patch
of dead grass and nothing.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.450
Well,something turned that
grave into unholy ground.

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.000
There's no reason for
it to be unholy ground.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.309
Angela mason was a nice
girl who died in a car crash.

00:18:55.309 --> 00:18:57.750
That's not exactly
vengeful-Spirit material.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.309
You heard her father.

00:18:59.309 --> 00:19:03.100
Maybe daddy doesn't know  everything
there is to know about his little angel,

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:06.400
You know what? We never should
have bothered that poor man.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.140
We shouldn't even be here anymore.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:12.210
So,what,sam?We just bail without
even figuring out what's going on?

00:19:13.079 --> 00:19:15.370
I think I know what's going on here.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:18.050
It's the only reason I went
along with you this far.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:21.260
What are you talking about?
This is about mom's grave.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:24.360
Got nothing to do with it.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:27.480
You wouldn't step
within 100 yards of it.

00:19:28.039 --> 00:19:31.059
Look,maybe you're imagining
a hunt where there isn't one

00:19:31.059 --> 00:19:34.900
So you don't have to
think about mom or dad.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.809
You want to take another swing? Go ahead

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.300
If it will make you feel better.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.789
I don't need this crap.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:58.690
Dean,where are you going?

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:00.360
I'm gonna go get a drink...

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.280
Alone.

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:58.160
Who the hell are you?!
Wait,wait,wait,wait.

00:21:58.160 --> 00:21:59.650
Hold on!

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:01.190
I'm calling 911!

00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:03.740
'M angela's cousin. What?

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:07.030
Yeah,her dad sent me
over to pick up her stuff.

00:22:07.030 --> 00:22:10.360
My name's alan
-- Alan stanwick.

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:16.480
Her dad didn't say that you were coming.

00:22:17.059 --> 00:22:19.410
Well,I mean...

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:23.490
How else would I have
the key to your place?

00:22:32.789 --> 00:22:39.140
So,I'm sure you got a view of angela
that none of the family got to see.

00:22:39.140 --> 00:22:41.210
Tell me,what was she like?

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:42.809
What was she really like?

00:22:42.809 --> 00:22:44.800
She was great...

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:48.260
Just...great.

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:50.840
I mean,she was so...

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:54.590
Great.

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:57.039
Yeah.

00:22:57.539 --> 00:22:59.880
Yeah.

00:23:03.269 --> 00:23:06.190
You two must have been really close,huh?

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:09.670
We were.

00:23:10.190 --> 00:23:12.230
But it's not just her, it's matt.

00:23:12.710 --> 00:23:14.210
Who?

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:15.809
Angela's boyfriend.

00:23:15.809 --> 00:23:17.910
Right -Matt.

00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:19.760
Uh,what about him?

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.289
He killed himself last night.

00:23:22.289 --> 00:23:25.550
He cut his own throat. Who does that?

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:28.840
That'S...terrible.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:33.000
He was taking angela's death
pretty hard,and I guess...

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:37.890
I mean,he'd been messed
up about it for days.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:39.130
Messed up how?

00:23:39.130 --> 00:23:42.019
He kept saying that
he saw her everywhere.

00:23:42.019 --> 00:23:43.940
Well,I'm -- I'm
sure that's normal.

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:45.900
I mean,with everything
he was going through.

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:48.610
He said that he saw her...

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:51.769
As in an acid trip or something.

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:55.230
Were angela and matt a happy couple?

00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:57.990
I mean,was there any reason that
angela would be angry with him?

00:23:57.990 --> 00:23:59.769
What?

00:23:59.769 --> 00:24:02.530
No,of course not. Why do you ask?

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:05.610
Just asking.

00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:09.329
Where did matt live?

00:24:09.329 --> 00:24:11.260
Next on cinemax,

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:13.360
"Casa erotica iv,"

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:16.380
A tale of two latin beauties,

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:19.559
Hey.

00:24:22.269 --> 00:24:23.930
What?

00:24:23.930 --> 00:24:25.809
Awkward.

00:24:25.809 --> 00:24:28.600
Where the hell were you? Just
working my imaginary case.

00:24:29.809 --> 00:24:31.700
Yeah? And?

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:34.490
Oh,well,you were right.
I didn't find much.

00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:37.420
Yeah. Except angela's
boyfriend died last night --

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:40.030
Slit his own throat,
but,you know,that's normal.

00:24:40.470 --> 00:24:41.370
Uh,let's see. What else?

00:24:41.370 --> 00:24:45.200
Oh,he was seeing angela
everywhere before he died.

00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:48.530
But,you know,I'm sure  that's just
me transferring my own feelings.

00:24:48.530 --> 00:24:50.079
Okay,I get it.

00:24:50.079 --> 00:24:51.910
I'm sorry. Maybe there is
something going on here.

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:53.559
Maybe?

00:24:53.559 --> 00:24:57.559
Sam,I know how to do my job
despite what you might think.

00:24:59.100 --> 00:25:01.440
We should check out the guy's apartment.

00:25:01.860 --> 00:25:04.000
I just came from there...

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.930
A pile of dead plants
just like the cemetery.

00:25:06.930 --> 00:25:08.690
Hell,a dead goldfish,too.

00:25:08.690 --> 00:25:11.380
So,unholy ground? Maybe.

00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:15.360
I'm still not getting that powerful
angry-Spirit vibe from angela.

00:25:15.940 --> 00:25:17.930
I've been reading this, though.

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:26.200
You stole the girl's diary? Yeah,sam.

00:25:27.570 --> 00:25:29.550
And if anything, the
girl's a little too nice.

00:25:29.550 --> 00:25:30.970
So,what do you want to do?

00:25:30.970 --> 00:25:32.760
Keep digging, talk to
more of her friends.

00:25:32.760 --> 00:25:35.289
You get any names? You kidding me?

00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:38.670
I have her bestest friend
in the whole wide world.

00:25:40.660 --> 00:25:43.269
I didn't realize the college
employed grief counselors.

00:25:43.269 --> 00:25:44.460
Oh,yeah.

00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:46.170
Yeah,you talk,we listen

00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:50.280
And maybe throw in a little therapeutic
collage whatever helps jump-Start the healing.

00:25:50.280 --> 00:25:53.559
Well,I think I'm okay. Thanks.

00:25:53.559 --> 00:25:56.500
Well,you heard what happened
to matt harrison,right?

00:25:56.500 --> 00:25:57.880
Yeah,I did.

00:25:57.880 --> 00:26:00.630
We just wanted to make
sure you were okay.

00:26:00.630 --> 00:26:04.030
Grief can make people do crazy things.

00:26:05.680 --> 00:26:09.370
Look,I'm sorry about
what happened to him.I am.

00:26:09.370 --> 00:26:12.340
But if matt killed himself,
it wasn't 'cause of grief.

00:26:12.340 --> 00:26:14.039
No? Then why?

00:26:14.039 --> 00:26:16.070
It was guilt.

00:26:16.070 --> 00:26:18.420
Angie's death was matt's
fault, and he knew it.

00:26:18.420 --> 00:26:20.269
How was matt responsible?

00:26:20.269 --> 00:26:22.690
She really loved that guy,

00:26:22.690 --> 00:26:26.269
But the night of the accident, she
walked in on him with another girl.

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:31.550
She was really torn up.
That's why she crashed.

00:26:33.530 --> 00:26:35.019
Um,look, I got to get ready for work,

00:26:35.019 --> 00:26:40.440
So thanks for the concern,
but,seriously,I'll be okay.

00:26:45.850 --> 00:26:48.330
Well,my vengeful-Spirit theory is
starting to make a little more sense.

00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:50.930
I mean,hell hath no fury.

00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:55.000
So,if angela got her revenge
on matt,you think it's over?

00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:58.440
Well, there's one way to be sure.

00:27:00.170 --> 00:27:02.390
Yeah? What's that?

00:27:02.780 --> 00:27:04.400
Burn the bones.

00:27:04.400 --> 00:27:06.460
Burn the bones?

00:27:06.910 --> 00:27:10.540
Are you high? Angela died last week.

00:27:10.540 --> 00:27:11.900
So?

00:27:11.900 --> 00:27:16.490
So there's not gonna be bones. There's
gonna be a ripe,rotting body in the coffin.

00:27:16.490 --> 00:27:19.460
Since when are you
afraid to get dirty,huh?

00:27:45.290 --> 00:27:47.140
Ladies first.

00:27:50.170 --> 00:27:52.090
Hold that.

00:28:27.759 --> 00:28:30.320
I missed you.

00:28:52.759 --> 00:28:54.800
They buried the body four days ago.

00:28:54.800 --> 00:28:57.269
I don't get it.

00:28:57.269 --> 00:28:58.860
Look.

00:29:02.580 --> 00:29:04.740
What is that? I'm not sure.

00:29:05.230 --> 00:29:07.810
I've seen these kinds of symbols before.

00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:13.690
Dean,take it easy,okay?

00:29:20.830 --> 00:29:22.470
You're angie's friends.

00:29:22.470 --> 00:29:25.000
Dr. Mason --
We need to talk.

00:29:25.810 --> 00:29:27.540
Well,come in.

00:29:28.519 --> 00:29:30.019
Thanks.

00:29:33.140 --> 00:29:35.269
You teach ancient greek.

00:29:35.269 --> 00:29:37.290
Tell me...

00:29:37.670 --> 00:29:39.750
What are these?

00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:43.280
I don't understand.

00:29:43.280 --> 00:29:46.019
You said this had
something to do with angela.

00:29:46.019 --> 00:29:49.150
It does. Please,just humor me.

00:29:51.110 --> 00:29:54.120
They're part of an ancient
greek divination ritual.

00:29:54.120 --> 00:29:56.640
Used for necromancy,right. That's right.

00:29:56.640 --> 00:29:57.759
See, before we came over here,

00:29:57.759 --> 00:30:00.940
We stopped by the library and
did a little homework ourselves.

00:30:00.940 --> 00:30:05.080
Apparently, they use rituals like this
one for communicating with the dead,

00:30:05.080 --> 00:30:08.970
Even bringing corpses back to
life -Full-On zombie action.

00:30:08.970 --> 00:30:10.880
Yeah.

00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:14.140
I mean, according to the legends.

00:30:15.450 --> 00:30:17.100
Now,what's this all about?

00:30:17.100 --> 00:30:19.160
I think you know. Dean.

00:30:19.600 --> 00:30:21.190
Look,I get it.

00:30:21.190 --> 00:30:24.390
There are people that I would
give anything to see again,

00:30:24.390 --> 00:30:25.560
But what gives you the right?

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:26.810
Dean. What are you talking about?

00:30:26.810 --> 00:30:28.370
What's dead should stay dead! What?

00:30:28.370 --> 00:30:30.830
Stop it! What you brought
back isn't your daughter!

00:30:30.830 --> 00:30:33.350
These things are
vicious, they're violent!

00:30:33.350 --> 00:30:35.500
They're so nasty, they
rot the ground around them.

00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:38.190
I mean,come on! Haven't
you seen "pet sematary"?

00:30:38.190 --> 00:30:40.800
You're insane.

00:30:41.200 --> 00:30:44.030
Where is she? Get out of my house.

00:30:44.030 --> 00:30:46.300
I know you're hiding her
somewhere. Where is she?!

00:30:46.300 --> 00:30:48.610
Dean,stop! That's
enough. Dean,look --

00:30:48.610 --> 00:30:52.830
Beautiful,living plants. We're leaving.

00:30:52.830 --> 00:30:55.000
I'm calling the police. Sir,we're sorry.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.660
We won't bother you again.

00:31:01.120 --> 00:31:02.690
What the hell's the
matter with you? Back off.

00:31:02.690 --> 00:31:05.030
That man is innocent.
He didn't deserve that.

00:31:05.030 --> 00:31:07.290
So she's not here. Maybe he's
keeping her somewhere else.

00:31:07.290 --> 00:31:09.450
Stop it! That's enough,okay? Enough!

00:31:09.450 --> 00:31:11.800
Sam,I know what I'm doing.
No,you don'T...at all.

00:31:13.070 --> 00:31:15.320
I don't scare easy,but you're
scaring the crap out of me.

00:31:15.320 --> 00:31:16.790
Don't be overdramatic, sam.

00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:18.740
You're lucky this turned
out to be a real case,

00:31:18.740 --> 00:31:21.830
'Cause if it wasn't,you would've
found something else to kill.

00:31:21.830 --> 00:31:23.720
You're on edge, you're erratic,

00:31:23.720 --> 00:31:26.530
Except for when you're hunting,'cause
then you're downright scary.

00:31:26.530 --> 00:31:28.519
You're tailspinning,man,

00:31:28.519 --> 00:31:32.030
And you refuse to talk about it,
and you won't let me help you.

00:31:32.030 --> 00:31:33.519
I can take care of myself, thanks.

00:31:33.519 --> 00:31:35.400
No,you can't!

00:31:35.400 --> 00:31:38.670
And you're the only one who
thinks you should have to.

00:31:38.670 --> 00:31:41.070
You don't have to handle
this on your own. No one can.

00:31:41.070 --> 00:31:44.820
If you bring up dad's death one more
time -- Dean,it's killing you. Please.

00:31:47.330 --> 00:31:50.009
We've already lost dad.

00:31:50.009 --> 00:31:51.850
We lost mom.

00:31:51.850 --> 00:31:54.880
I've lost jessica.

00:31:54.880 --> 00:31:57.840
And now I'm gonna lose you,too?

00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:02.230
We better get out of
here before the cops come.

00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:05.840
I hear you,okay?

00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:08.570
I'm being an ass, and I'm sorry.

00:32:08.570 --> 00:32:12.310
But we got a freakin' zombie running
around. We need to figure out how to kill it.

00:32:15.300 --> 00:32:17.050
Right?

00:32:17.050 --> 00:32:19.470
Our lives are weird,man.

00:32:19.470 --> 00:32:21.750
You're telling me.

00:32:22.700 --> 00:32:25.300
Come on.

00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:29.370
Honey, is something bothering you?

00:32:30.940 --> 00:32:32.790
It's about matt.

00:32:32.790 --> 00:32:34.640
Haven't we already talked about that?

00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:35.840
I
know,but,uh --

00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:39.400
Haven't we wasted enough
time on him already?

00:32:40.140 --> 00:32:43.110
Come sit down.

00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:53.650
You always said that
he didn't deserve me.

00:32:54.259 --> 00:32:56.900
You were right. Angela...

00:32:59.330 --> 00:33:03.080
You didn't get out and go see matt or...

00:33:03.080 --> 00:33:05.259
I've been here the whole time.

00:33:06.970 --> 00:33:11.519
Neal...you really think I
could do something like that?

00:33:11.519 --> 00:33:14.230
No,I... I don't know.

00:33:14.970 --> 00:33:17.780
I can't help it. You just -You seem...

00:33:17.780 --> 00:33:19.650
Different?

00:33:20.550 --> 00:33:23.640
You're right. I am.

00:33:26.300 --> 00:33:29.030
I've realized...

00:33:29.030 --> 00:33:32.590
You're the only one who
ever really loved me.

00:33:34.570 --> 00:33:39.060
You proved that. You brought me back.

00:33:39.060 --> 00:33:41.560
I'm with you now.

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:45.700
Isn't that what you always wanted?

00:33:48.730 --> 00:33:50.990
We can't just waste
her with a head shot?

00:33:50.990 --> 00:33:53.810
Dude,you've been wahing
way too many romero flicks.

00:33:53.810 --> 00:33:55.910
You're telling me there's
no lore on how to smoke them?

00:33:55.910 --> 00:33:58.230
No,I'm telling you there's too much.

00:33:58.230 --> 00:34:00.310
There's 100 different
legends on the walking dead,

00:34:00.310 --> 00:34:02.210
But they all have different
methods for killing them.

00:34:02.210 --> 00:34:06.630
Some say setting them on
fire. One said -Where is it?

00:34:06.630 --> 00:34:08.989
Right here -Feeding
their hearts to wild dogs.

00:34:08.989 --> 00:34:10.820
That's my personal favorite.

00:34:10.820 --> 00:34:12.480
But who knows what's
real and what's myth?

00:34:12.480 --> 00:34:14.060
Is there anything they have in common?

00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:16.289
No,but a few said silver might work.

00:34:16.289 --> 00:34:17.780
Silver's a start.

00:34:17.780 --> 00:34:19.510
But now how are we going to find angela?

00:34:19.510 --> 00:34:21.190
We got to figure out
who brought her back.

00:34:21.190 --> 00:34:22.810
Any ideas?

00:34:22.810 --> 00:34:25.860
I think if it's not her dad,
it might be that guy,neal.

00:34:25.860 --> 00:34:27.260
Neal? Yep.

00:34:27.260 --> 00:34:30.030
How'd you come up with that?
Well,you got your journal,I got mine.

00:34:31.329 --> 00:34:32.840
"Neal's a real shoulder to cry on.

00:34:32.840 --> 00:34:36.630
He so understands what I'm
going through with matt."

00:34:36.630 --> 00:34:40.720
There's more here where that came from. It's
got unrequited duckie love written all over it.

00:34:40.720 --> 00:34:43.199
But that doesn't mean he
brought her back from the dead.

00:34:43.199 --> 00:34:45.730
Hmm,did I mention that
he's professor mason's T.A.?

00:34:45.730 --> 00:34:48.659
Has access to all the same books.

00:34:54.100 --> 00:34:55.900
Hello?

00:34:59.380 --> 00:35:01.400
Neal!

00:35:02.039 --> 00:35:04.800
It's your grief counselors.
We've come to hug.

00:35:08.369 --> 00:35:09.829
Silver bullets?

00:35:09.829 --> 00:35:13.030
Yeah,enough to make her
rattle like a change purse.

00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:41.680
Unless it's where he keeps his porn.

00:36:09.550 --> 00:36:12.090
It sure looks like a zombie pen to me.

00:36:12.090 --> 00:36:13.500
Yeah.

00:36:13.970 --> 00:36:16.039
An empty one.

00:36:17.480 --> 00:36:20.400
You think angela's gone after somebody?

00:36:29.829 --> 00:36:31.890
No,I think she went
out to rent "beaches."

00:36:31.890 --> 00:36:34.960
Look,smartass. She might kill someone.

00:36:34.960 --> 00:36:37.199
We got to find her,dean.

00:36:37.650 --> 00:36:39.820
Yeah.

00:36:40.380 --> 00:36:43.360
All right,she clipped matt
because he was cheating,right?

00:36:43.360 --> 00:36:44.360
Yeah.

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:49.130
Well,takes two to,you
know, have hard-Core sex.

00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:51.070
I don't know. It just seemed

00:36:51.070 --> 00:36:53.600
That angela's roommate was...

00:36:53.600 --> 00:36:56.739
Broken up over matt's death.

00:36:57.180 --> 00:37:01.500
I mean, like really broken up.

00:37:19.480 --> 00:37:21.650
Hello?

00:37:29.380 --> 00:37:31.470
Hi,lindsay. I'm home.

00:37:40.659 --> 00:37:42.650
You know what you did.

00:37:45.470 --> 00:37:46.619
I'm sorry!

00:37:46.619 --> 00:37:48.210
I am so sorry!

00:37:48.210 --> 00:37:50.030
Not sorry enough!

00:38:12.600 --> 00:38:13.769
God.

00:38:15.449 --> 00:38:17.140
God.

00:38:17.140 --> 00:38:18.610
Oh,my god.

00:38:18.610 --> 00:38:19.869
Oh,my god.

00:38:50.329 --> 00:38:51.869
I got you. I got you.

00:38:55.039 --> 00:38:57.110
Damn, that dead chick can run.

00:38:57.110 --> 00:38:59.350
What now?

00:38:59.850 --> 00:39:02.269
I say we go have a
little chat with neal.

00:39:05.970 --> 00:39:08.980
So,the silver bullets,
they did something,right?

00:39:08.980 --> 00:39:12.460
Yeah,something,but not
enough. What else you got?

00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:15.030
Um,okay,besides silver,

00:39:15.030 --> 00:39:18.500
We have "nailing the undead
back into their grave beds."

00:39:18.500 --> 00:39:22.860
It's mentioned a few times. It's probably
where the whole vampire-Staking lore came from.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:25.060
Their grave beds? You serious?

00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:26.090
Yeah.

00:39:26.090 --> 00:39:29.300
How the hell are we gonna get
angela back to the cemetery?

00:39:40.789 --> 00:39:42.769
What are you guys doing here?

00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:47.539
You know,I've heard of some people doing
some pretty desperate things to get laid,

00:39:47.539 --> 00:39:49.260
But you

00:39:49.260 --> 00:39:51.440
You take the cake.

00:39:51.440 --> 00:39:53.030
Okay,who are you guys?

00:39:53.030 --> 00:39:55.380
You might want to ask
angela that question.

00:39:55.380 --> 00:39:57.519
What? We know what you did.

00:39:58.630 --> 00:40:01.630
The ritual...everything.

00:40:03.070 --> 00:40:04.489
You're crazy.

00:40:04.489 --> 00:40:07.820
Your girlfriend's past her
expiration date, and we're crazy?

00:40:08.210 --> 00:40:10.949
When someone's gone,
they should stay gone.

00:40:10.949 --> 00:40:13.860
You don't mess with that kind of stuff.

00:40:13.860 --> 00:40:16.110
Angela killed matt.

00:40:16.110 --> 00:40:19.050
She tried to kill lindsay.

00:40:19.050 --> 00:40:22.329
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:40:24.460 --> 00:40:26.390
Hey,no more crap,neal!

00:40:26.390 --> 00:40:28.860
This blood is on your hands.

00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:32.710
Now,me and him can make this right,
but you got to tell us where she is.

00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:35.380
Tell us!

00:40:37.530 --> 00:40:39.500
My house.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:41.500
She's at my house.

00:40:51.650 --> 00:40:53.980
You sure about that?

00:41:03.659 --> 00:41:05.909
Listen. It doesn't really
matter where she is.

00:41:07.110 --> 00:41:09.640
There's only one way to stop her.

00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:14.190
We've got to perform another ritual over
her grave  to reverse the one that you did.

00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:18.140
We're going to need some black
roots, some scar weed,some candles.

00:41:18.140 --> 00:41:20.140
It's very complicated, but
it will get the job done.

00:41:20.140 --> 00:41:22.630
She'll be dead again in a couple hours.

00:41:22.630 --> 00:41:24.860
I think you should come with us.

00:41:28.250 --> 00:41:31.920
I'm serious,neal.
Leave with us right now.

00:41:31.920 --> 00:41:33.610
No.

00:41:34.369 --> 00:41:36.289
No.

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:43.199
Listen to me.

00:41:43.199 --> 00:41:45.550
Get out of here as soon as you can.

00:41:46.610 --> 00:41:50.539
But most of all,be cool.
No sudden movements.

00:41:50.539 --> 00:41:53.510
Don't make her mad.

00:41:56.409 --> 00:41:57.920
Let's go.

00:42:14.590 --> 00:42:16.390
You said you'd stay in the house.

00:42:16.390 --> 00:42:19.750
I'm sorry. I just needed to see you.

00:42:20.030 --> 00:42:22.519
Neal,please.

00:42:24.650 --> 00:42:27.570
You have to help me.

00:42:30.269 --> 00:42:31.890
Oh,god.

00:42:31.890 --> 00:42:35.280
Come with me to the cemetery.
Neal,they're trying to kill me.

00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:36.810
We have to stop them.

00:42:36.810 --> 00:42:38.970
You mean kill them?

00:42:40.269 --> 00:42:42.260
It's
true --

00:42:42.260 --> 00:42:45.280
Matt and lindsay. They hurt me.

00:42:45.970 --> 00:42:49.070
If you love me,you'll make
sure nobody hurts me again.

00:42:49.070 --> 00:42:52.480
Take me to the cemetery,
then all this will be over.

00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:55.650
We can start new lives together.

00:42:57.739 --> 00:42:59.720
Okay.

00:43:00.980 --> 00:43:03.619
God help me,but okay.

00:43:04.409 --> 00:43:06.750
I'll go get the car.

00:43:06.750 --> 00:43:08.180
Just...

00:43:08.180 --> 00:43:10.350
Just wait here.

00:43:33.639 --> 00:43:35.630
Neal,you look nervous.

00:43:36.200 --> 00:43:38.300
No,I'm fine.

00:43:39.590 --> 00:43:42.599
Were you... going to leave me?

00:43:43.030 --> 00:43:44.590
No,of course not.

00:43:44.590 --> 00:43:46.930
You were,weren't you?!

00:43:46.930 --> 00:43:50.300
How could you?! Neal,I loved you!

00:43:50.300 --> 00:43:51.530
Angela
--

00:44:04.269 --> 00:44:06.840
You really think this is gonna work?

00:44:06.840 --> 00:44:09.420
No,not really.

00:44:11.440 --> 00:44:14.240
But it was the only thing
I could come up with.

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:12.490
Wait. It's not what you think.

00:45:12.490 --> 00:45:15.760
I didn't ask to be brought
back, but it's still me.

00:45:15.760 --> 00:45:18.789
I'm still a person. Please.

00:45:54.740 --> 00:45:56.789
Please don't!

00:46:13.579 --> 00:46:16.119
What's dead should stay dead.

00:46:24.460 --> 00:46:25.829
Rest in peace.

00:46:25.829 --> 00:46:27.990
Yeah, for good this time,okay?

00:46:34.440 --> 00:46:36.110
You know,

00:46:36.519 --> 00:46:38.280
The whole fake-Ritual thing,

00:46:38.280 --> 00:46:42.150
Luring angela into the
cemetery -Pretty sharp.

00:46:42.150 --> 00:46:44.079
Thanks.

00:46:44.079 --> 00:46:46.660
But did we have to use me as bait?

00:46:46.660 --> 00:46:50.519
I figured you were more her type,you
know? She had pretty crappy taste in guys.

00:46:50.930 --> 00:46:53.099
I think she broke my hand.

00:46:53.599 --> 00:46:56.920
You're just too fragile.
We'll get it looked at later.

00:47:02.309 --> 00:47:04.519
You want to stay for a while?

00:47:09.230 --> 00:47:11.320
No.

00:48:18.750 --> 00:48:20.809
Dean,what is it?

00:48:24.860 --> 00:48:26.329
I'm sorry.

00:48:27.849 --> 00:48:29.809
For what?

00:48:31.539 --> 00:48:34.170
The way I've been acting.

00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:54.240
And for dad.

00:48:56.680 --> 00:48:59.829
Well, he was your dad,too.

00:49:00.619 --> 00:49:02.420
It's my fault that he's gone.

00:49:02.420 --> 00:49:04.300
What are you talking about?

00:49:04.300 --> 00:49:07.250
I know you've been
thinking it. So have I.

00:49:08.070 --> 00:49:10.610
Doesn't take a genius to figure it out.

00:49:11.990 --> 00:49:16.280
Back at the hospital,
I had a full recovery.

00:49:16.280 --> 00:49:19.059
It was a miracle.

00:49:19.059 --> 00:49:21.820
And five minutes later, dad's
dead,and the colt's gone.

00:49:21.820 --> 00:49:25.470
You can't tell me there's
not a connection there.

00:49:27.300 --> 00:49:30.340
I don't know how the demon was involved.

00:49:30.829 --> 00:49:34.329
I don't know how the whole
thing went down exactly...

00:49:34.880 --> 00:49:38.440
But dad's dead because of me.

00:49:38.440 --> 00:49:40.059
And that much I do know.

00:49:40.059 --> 00:49:42.460
We don't know that, not for sure.

00:49:42.460 --> 00:49:45.450
Sam...

00:49:46.710 --> 00:49:50.730
You and dad...

00:49:51.970 --> 00:49:54.950
You're the most important
people in my life.

00:49:55.380 --> 00:49:59.019
And now...

00:49:59.420 --> 00:50:02.990
I never should have come
back, sam. It wasn't natural.

00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:07.329
And now look what's come of it.

00:50:09.639 --> 00:50:11.900
I was dead.

00:50:13.039 --> 00:50:16.519
And I should have stayed dead.

00:50:22.139 --> 00:50:25.220
You wanted to know how I was feeling.

00:50:26.710 --> 00:50:29.480
Well,that's it.

00:50:31.950 --> 00:50:33.980
So tell me.

00:50:38.680 --> 00:50:42.269
What could you possibly
say to make that all right?



00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.650
